    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0412" n="312" xml:id="pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-09T18:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1934—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. You may in your discretion join with the British Ambassador Berlin,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d250-f1"/> who it is understood has received similar
                    instructions, in supporting proposal of James G. McDonald that he be enabled to
                    negotiate with an authorized representative of the Reich concerning transfer of
                    moneys involving (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) income for living expenditures
                    of refugees, and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) some capital for purposes of
                    establishment, as well as the question of insurance and pensions owing to former
                    Government functionaries, including professors. If the Germans take the position
                    that this is entirely a domestic matter, you may point out that German citizens
                    are becoming in one way or another public charges on foreign countries. We leave
                    to you and Phipps the decision as to the best time and manner of approaching the
                    German authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d250-f1" n="11" xml:id="d250-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Eric Clare Edmund Phipps.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
